<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Hassan II of Morocco</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates"><a href="/years/1929">1929</a>–<a href="/years/1999">1999</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/20th-century">20th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Hassan II was King of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/morocco">Morocco</a> from 1961 until his death in 1999, of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/alaouite-dynasty">Alaouite dynasty</a>. He introduced constitutions but kept firm power, surviving military coup attempts in 1971 and 1972 and repressing opponents during the period known as the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/years-of-lead-italy">Years of Lead</a>. In 1975 he organised the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/green-march">Green March</a> into <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/western-sahara">Western Sahara</a>, which Morocco then annexed.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/hassan-ii-of-morocco.jpg" alt="Hassan II of Morocco" width="320" height="449" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Christian Lambiotte · CC BY 4.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Hassan_II_(1983).jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
